 <longdesc><para unique="1261284">BNDMOV moves a pair of lower and upper bound values from the source operand (the second operand) to the destination (the first operand). Each operation is 128-bit move. The exceptions are same as the MOV instruction. The memory format for loading/store bounds in 64-bit mode is shown in <link unique="1261286" linkend="#34586: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 10-8. Layout of the Bounds Registers BND0-BND3" xrefstyle="FigureNum">Figure&#160;3&#8209;5</link>.</para>
  <figure id="34586: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 10-8. Layout of the Bounds Registers BND0-BND3"><title>Memory Layout of BNDMOV to/from Memory</title>
